CXPP-SECRET-SCAN-COVERAGE-MARKER-V1

This file is a NEGATIVE CONTROL for the secret scanner, not configuration. It
carries a benign marker that the coverage probe in .woodpecker.yml requires the
repository scan to report, using the production .gitleaks.toml plus one extra
rule that makes this token detectable.

Its purpose is to make one specific silent failure loud: the scan can be
narrowed to stop examining a directory - by a path entry in .gitleaks.toml's
allowlist - and nothing about the scan's output would change, because a scan
that examines less still reports "no leaks found". Exclude the directory this
file is in, and the probe stops finding this marker and fails.

Deleting or emptying this file is a weakening. tests/test_gitleaks_allowlist.py
requires it to exist and to carry the token, and names the directories that need
one: the repository root, and every directory an allowlist path entry names.
